<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>ioq3 — PC WASM remaster</title>
  <script>
    // Claim loading before window.load; the injected SDK otherwise auto-readies.
    window.OG?.loading?.begin?.(['Engine', 'Settings', 'Assets', 'World']);
    if (window.OG?.embedded) document.documentElement.dataset.embedded = 'true';
  </script>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="./shell.css">
</head>
<body data-engine="./@CLIENT_BINARY@.js" data-state="loading">
  <!-- SDL2's Emscripten backend requires the literal #canvas selector. -->
  <canvas id="canvas" tabindex="0" aria-label="ioq3 game canvas"></canvas>
  <main id="status-panel" aria-labelledby="title">
    <p class="eyebrow">PC BROWSER · WASM / WEBGL2</p>
    <h1 id="title">BUILT FOR<br>THE ARENA.</h1>
    <p id="status" role="status" aria-live="polite">Loading engine…</p>
    <p id="detail">Preparing the browser runtime.</p>
    <button id="retry" hidden>Reload and retry</button>
    <p class="note">Game data must be installed by the build owner. The engine alone is not a playable game.</p>
  </main>
  <section id="menu" aria-label="Arena menu" hidden>
    <header><span class="eyebrow">IOQ3 / REMASTER PROGRAM</span><span class="badge">PC · WEBGL2</span></header>
    <div class="menu-layout">
      <nav class="menu-nav" aria-label="Main navigation">
        <p class="eyebrow">OPERATIONS</p>
        <button data-screen="home" aria-current="page">01 / Overview</button>
        <button data-screen="settings">02 / Settings</button>
        <button data-screen="display">03 / Display</button>
        <button data-screen="bindings">04 / Key bindings</button>
        <button data-screen="profile">05 / Player profile</button>
        <button data-screen="help">06 / Field manual</button>
        <button id="return-engine">Return to engine</button>
      </nav>
      <div class="menu-content">
        <section data-page="home">
          <p class="eyebrow" id="menu-context">ARENA SYSTEMS / ONLINE</p>
          <h2 id="menu-title" tabindex="-1">MAKE EVERY<br>MOVE COUNT.</h2>
          <p class="intro">Precision in motion. No shortcuts.</p>
          <button class="primary" id="play">Open engine Play menu →</button>
          <p class="note" id="play-note">Map, bot and match selection currently use the original engine menu.</p>
          <div class="availability"><span>Multiplayer</span><p>Room entry requires a platform-issued session. No public lobby is configured in this build.</p></div>
        </section>
        <section data-page="settings" hidden>
          <p class="eyebrow">TUNE YOUR RESPONSE</p><h2 tabindex="-1">SETTINGS</h2>
          <p class="note">Changes apply immediately in the engine. Archived settings save automatically on an engine frame, then sync to this browser.</p>
          <div id="setting-fields"></div>
          <p id="setting-status" class="edit-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
          <p class="note">FOV becomes available after entering a map. Use Display for live filtering and crosshair controls; Key bindings for action assignments.</p>
        </section>
        <section data-page="display" class="config-page" hidden>
          <p class="eyebrow">IMAGE / READABILITY</p><h2 tabindex="-1">DISPLAY</h2>
          <label class="setting-row">Texture filtering<select id="texture-filter"><option value="-2" disabled>Custom / unavailable</option><option value="0">Nearest mipmap</option><option value="1">Bilinear</option><option value="2">Trilinear</option></select></label>
          <div id="display-fields"></div>
          <p class="edit-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
          <p class="note">Filtering updates existing world textures without restart. Crosshair 0 is off; 1–10 select engine shapes. Crosshair/FPS controls require a loaded map. Spectator and gameplay rules may hide the crosshair.</p>
          <p class="note">Resolution and texture detail require renderer restart with recovery; those remain in the engine menu. Browser gamma is not offered as a misleading live brightness control.</p>
        </section>
        <section data-page="bindings" class="config-page" hidden>
          <p class="eyebrow">INPUT / ACTIONS</p><h2 tabindex="-1">KEY BINDINGS</h2>
          <p class="note">Change or clear individual slots; additional existing bindings are preserved. Esc, console, F10–F12 and OS-reserved shortcuts stay outside this editor. Custom command bindings cannot be overwritten.</p>
          <p class="list-caption">30 actions · Scroll the list for weapons and advanced controls ↓</p>
          <div id="binding-fields" class="binding-list" tabindex="0" aria-label="Scrollable action bindings"></div>
          <div id="binding-conflict" hidden><p id="binding-conflict-text"></p><button id="binding-replace">Replace conflicting action</button><button id="binding-cancel">Cancel</button></div>
          <p class="edit-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
        </section>
        <section data-page="profile" class="config-page" hidden>
          <p class="eyebrow">IDENTITY / PLAYER</p><h2 tabindex="-1">PLAYER PROFILE</h2>
          <form id="profile-form"><label class="setting-row">Player name<input id="player-name" required minlength="1" maxlength="31" autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false"></label><button type="submit">Apply name</button></form>
          <p class="note">1–31 printable ASCII characters; at most three consecutive spaces. No leading/trailing spaces, color escapes, quotes, semicolons or backslashes. Existing names are never silently rewritten.</p>
          <div id="profile-fields"></div>
          <p class="note">Colors: 1 blue · 2 green · 3 cyan · 4 red · 5 magenta · 6 yellow · 7 white. Lower handicap limits health. Model/skin selection still uses the original engine's installed-content catalogue.</p>
          <p class="edit-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
        </section>
        <section data-page="help" hidden>
          <p class="eyebrow">FIELD MANUAL / PC</p><h2 tabindex="-1">STAY IN CONTROL.</h2>
          <dl><dt>F10</dt><dd>Open this menu without leaving the match.</dd><dt>Esc</dt><dd>Release mouse capture. Open the engine pause menu while playing.</dd><dt>Mouse capture</dt><dd>Use Capture mouse / enable sound after returning to the game.</dd><dt>Browser storage</dt><dd>Settings are local to this browser and origin. Clearing site data removes them.</dd><dt>Online matches</dt><dd>Opening a menu does not stop a remote match. Other players continue playing.</dd></dl>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
    <footer><span>ENGINE-NATIVE GAMEPLAY</span><span>WASM / PC EDITION</span></footer>
  </section>
  <nav id="controls" aria-label="Browser controls" hidden>
    <button id="open-menu">Menu / F10</button>
    <button id="capture">Capture mouse / enable sound</button>
    <button id="fullscreen">Enter fullscreen</button>
    <button id="exit-fullscreen">Exit fullscreen</button>
    <button id="save">Save settings</button>
    <span id="save-status" role="status"></span>
    <span id="input-status" role="status">Esc releases mouse</span>
    <span id="network-status" role="status"></span>
  </nav>
  <script type="module" src="./app.mjs"></script>
</body>
</html>
